<title>USA: Pa. officials plan upgrade for Delaware Canal Park.</title>
<headline>Pa. officials plan upgrade for Delaware Canal Park.</headline>
<dateline>DOYLESTOWN, Pa. 1997-08-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pennsylvania Conservation and Natural Resources officials unveiled a five-year plan to improve the Delaware Canal State Park.</p>
<p>The plan would cost $7.65 million and would focus on creating additional recreational opportunities at the park.</p>
<p>State funds would will help pay for the upgrades.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
